# AI English Tutor — environment variables (NAMES ONLY)
#
# Copy this file to `.env` (or `.env.local`) and fill in real values locally.
# `.env` and every `.env.*` file are gitignored; only this `.env.example`
# template is tracked. NEVER commit a real key.
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# WARNING — EXPO_PUBLIC_* IS NOT A SAFE PLACE FOR A PRODUCTION SECRET
#
# Expo inlines every `EXPO_PUBLIC_*` variable into the compiled JavaScript
# bundle as plain text. Anyone who installs the app can extract the value.
#
# `EXPO_PUBLIC_GEMINI_API_KEY` below is therefore a DEVELOPMENT CONVENIENCE
# ONLY. The app honours it only in a development/test build (`__DEV__ === true`)
# and IGNORES it entirely in a release build (`preview` / `production`).
#
# The production path is runtime configuration: open the app's Settings →
# "AI provider" and save the key there. It is kept in secure device storage
# (expo-secure-store), never in this file and never in the bundle.
# See README.md → "Runtime provider configuration".
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Development-only Google Gemini API key used by the AI (conversation/feedback)
# and speech-to-text providers while developing. Leave empty to run without one.
# Released builds ignore this value completely — configure the key in the app.
EXPO_PUBLIC_GEMINI_API_KEY=

# Optional: override the Gemini REST endpoint used by the providers.
# Leave empty to use the built-in default.
EXPO_PUBLIC_GEMINI_API_BASE_URL=
